From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Report a present card without applications as
 no SIM

A card is reported to oFono as inserted once it is present and has an
application, and as removed only when it goes absent. An eUICC whose
profile is disabled does neither: after the card has been reset it
comes back present, with no applications at all. oFono was never told,
and kept showing the old SIM as present, with its old provider name,
only no longer registered. Seen on a Brax3 after disabling an eUICC
profile: getIccCardStatus said card_state=1, num_apps=0, while oFono's
SimManager still had Present true.

Treat a card that is present but has no application oFono can use as
no SIM. Enabling a profile again then reports the SIM as inserted
again, as before.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/binder_sim.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/binder_sim.c b/src/binder_sim.c
index cfb4826..5610386 100644
--- a/src/binder_sim.c
+++ b/src/binder_sim.c
@@ -1162,25 +1162,28 @@ binder_sim_status_changed_cb(
     BinderSim* self = user_data;
 
     GASSERT(self->card == sim);
-    if (sim->status && sim->status->card_state == RADIO_CARD_STATE_PRESENT) {
-        if (sim->app) {
-            enum ofono_sim_password_type ps;
-
-            binder_sim_check_perm_lock(self);
-            if (!self->inserted) {
-                self->inserted = TRUE;
-                ofono_info("SIM card OK");
-                ofono_sim_inserted_notify(self->sim, TRUE);
-            }
+    if (sim->status && sim->status->card_state == RADIO_CARD_STATE_PRESENT &&
+        sim->app) {
+        enum ofono_sim_password_type ps;
+
+        binder_sim_check_perm_lock(self);
+        if (!self->inserted) {
+            self->inserted = TRUE;
+            ofono_info("SIM card OK");
+            ofono_sim_inserted_notify(self->sim, TRUE);
+        }
 
-            ps = binder_sim_passwd_state(self);
-            if (ps != OFONO_SIM_PASSWORD_INVALID) {
-                binder_sim_finish_passwd_state_query(self, ps);
-            }
-        } else {
-            binder_sim_invalidate_passwd_state(self);
+        ps = binder_sim_passwd_state(self);
+        if (ps != OFONO_SIM_PASSWORD_INVALID) {
+            binder_sim_finish_passwd_state_query(self, ps);
         }
     } else {
+        /*
+         * A card that is present but has no application oFono can use
+         * is no SIM to oFono either. An eUICC looks like that once its
+         * profile is disabled: the card never goes absent, only its
+         * applications go away, and oFono would keep the old SIM.
+         */
         binder_sim_invalidate_passwd_state(self);
         if (self->inserted) {
             self->inserted = FALSE;
